To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: ADDENDUM to SUCCESS: SCSI upgrade advice sought ......
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078618110759


Hi,

I was notified that I've swapped the "mkfset" and "mkfdmn" commands.
This is how it should be:

         # mkfdmn newroot_domain /dev/rz2a
         # mkfset newroot_domain root
         # mkfdmn newusr_domain /dev/rz2g
         # mkfset newusr_domain usr

One more thing, I've noticed today which may be required when copying
a system from one disk to the other: If you're using the automounter,
the copy process copies the /tmp_mnt directory as well. This confuses
the automounter after booting from the new system disk and causes it to
hang after automounting a file system.

So directly after copying the system disk, do a

         # rm -rf /mnt/root/tmp_mnt

in order to get it going properly.

Tom

