On my alpha MULTIA (to run under UNIX 4.0b) I changed the resolution of
the screen modifying the 4 central unnamed jumpers. Here the scheme of
all my tests:  (The 4 cells denotes the 4 jumpers as seen on the top of
the motherboard having the rear connectors on your side. The 1 means the
presence of jumper while the 0 means the absence of jumper)

00
00	1280x1024

00
10 	1280X1024

00
01	1280x1024

01
00	1024x768

10
00	1152x900

00
11	1152x900

11
00	640x480

01
01	800x600

01
10	800x600

10
01	1024x768

10
10	1024x768


Please note that to let Unix see the resolution of 1280x1024 I had to
install UNIX from CD with the jumper already set to such resolution.
(I did using the first configuration 0000)

Greatings, 
Emanuele


