I didn't receive any responses to this, but we found the answer from the
vendor.

The current legato client for NT was the problem (4.3).  We are assured
that this has been fixed in version 4.4.  This problem does not manifest
itself with Digital UNIX clients (probably because of directory file
structure).

Original posting:
>
>We have seen the following problem on NT Networker clients (apparently).
> Can anyone determine if it appears on Digital UNIX clients as well (or,
>even better, that it doesn't)?
>
>Scenario:
>
>files:
>C:\dira\suba\f1.dat
>C:\dira\suba\f2.dat
>
>Full backup is performed
>
>directory 'suba' is renamed to 'subb'
>
>now have files:
>C:\dira\suba\f1.dat
>C:\dira\suba\f2.dat
>
>Incremental is performed.
>
>Disk Crashes
>
>Restore the full disk using information up to and including latest
>incremental:
>
>have:
>
>C:\dira\subb   <But no files!!!!>
>
>This appears to be because the savegroup command (NSR Server) causes the
>save or savefs command (NSR Client) to be run with the '-t <date>'
>option which causes it only to back up files modified after the given
>date.  The files fil1.dat and fil2.dat were not modified after the full
>and so were not backed up.  The latest version of 'dira' does not
>include the directory 'suba' so that whole sub-tree is not restored.
>
>I would dearly hope that something in this scenario is incorrect but it
>is what we have pieced together so far.  Please let me know if you can
>confirm or refute this hypothesis.
