The problem was a hardware failure. My Original posting was


We have  a 4100 Server with Digital Unix 3.2g connected to a HSZ50
controll and Raid arrays. Last Sunday the system Crashed with the
following message:
ADVFS Internal error: Deallocate -bits-page
Can't clear a bit twice
ADVFS Exception
Module=19, Line=252
Sw_dmn#unidata inconsistancy detected.
Does not contain a valid ADVFS file system.

After reboot whenever system was mounting the HSZ disks it was Crashing
with following error:

System has halted due to an irrecoverable error
halt code=7
Machine check with PAL Mode
PC=14400
Call Digital Support.

The Local Digital support tried to change the SCSI KZPSA, checked the
CPU, memeory , but still we got the errors. Software support asked us to
recreate the raid sets and reload the data. It was completed on Monday
and we could read the disks, but the system crashed with ADVFS Exception
etc the first error as above.

