From: "Ramanujan, Preethi" <PRamanujan () iga ! com>
Date: Wed, 15 Oct 1997 15:22:50 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: LAT Printing on  ALpha Server 400 running Unix  4.0b
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078618110472


Hi  all,

Well  Dec  support  sorted out  the  problem  in  a  minute. When  I
changed  the  firmware  and  powered
on  the  terminal  server  I  had  forgotten  to  configure  the  name
for  the  terminal  server. (When  we  did  a  ---> show  server  the
name  which  showed  up  was  the  same  as  the  address  of  the
90L+)
Once  I  changed  the name of  90L+   Printing  is  working  fine . 

I  aso  want  to  thank  Jude  from  the  forum( jude@tsi.com.my.) for
the  immediate  response .  The  response  from  Jude  was as  follows:
Check your /etc/printcap file and make sure the following line`rw' is
removed. The explanation is that this tells lpd' to open the device in
read/write mode rather  than write  only mode.


Preethi


