We are running Oracle RDBMS 7.3.3.3 on DUNIX 4.0b (Patch Level #2).
Last week everything was running as expected with all Oracle processes
running at normal user levels.  Over the weekend, the database was
shutdown and a cold backup taken. The database was then restarted and
now all the Oracle processes are running with a nice level of 2.  There
are two questions here:

1) Is this a problem? Our lead Oracle DBA states that ALL Oracle
processes need to be
    run at the same process priority to prevent lockup problems.  He
also states that
    Oracle says NO Oracle processes should be "nice"d.  Has anyone seen
this problem
    and, if so, what was done to resolve it, if anything?

2) The last part of the question in part one is critical.  What causes
this to happen if nothing
    has changed as far as Oracle patches, systems patches, application
patches, etc. other
    than the database being brought down and then restarted?  Is there
something in DUNIX
