From: Graham_McKenzie () jabil ! com
Date: Wed, 08 Oct 1997 14:25:53 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY PART 2 : Sybae Can't find libsys5.so
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078618110318

     Apologies DEC managers but in my rush to get home last night I forgot 
     to include the definitive answer from johan M which goes something 
     like this :-
     
     grep libsys5.so /usr/.smdb./*.inv
     
     
     and this will tell you what subset the file belongs to.  So the above 
     command generates the following output
     
     /usr/.smdb./OSFSVID2410.inv:0   40960   34908   3       4       100644 
     11/15/96
     410     f       ./usr/opt/s5/usr/shlib/libsys5.so       none    
     OSFSVID2410     
     /usr/.smdb./OSFSVID2410.inv:0   30      00000   0       0       120777 
     11/18/96
     410     s       ./usr/shlib/libsys5.so  ../opt/s5/usr/shlib/libsys5.so 
     OSFSVID2
     410                                                                    
     
     
     As you can see from the above, the subset is OSFVID2410.
     
     Use the setld -l /cdrom/ALPHA/BASE command to load the corresponding 
     set (assuming /cdrom is your mount point). 
     
     Once again, apologies for any confusion caused
     
     Graham Mckenzie
     Jabil Circuit Inc.
     

