Hello Managers,

Yesterday i posted the following problem:

>I have a advfs problem.
>Yesterday i updated my 400 4/233 Alphastation from 3.2g up
>to 4.0a and then to 4.0b. The home partition is a 1 GByte
>harddisk on which i use and used advfs.
>On 3.2g i used the dxadvfs tool to manage this volume.
>For the update to 4.0b i deinstalled the old version of
>the advfs GUI and afterwards installed the AFAADVxxx402
>savesets. 
>Now, if i start dtadvfs the tool initializes, and the a window
>pops up where i have select the host (Host selection window).
>If i choose the hostname of my machine (given by the tool)
>and try connect the following error pops up:
>Failed to make agent connection to host ...

>I looked at the /var/opt/advfsd/socket/hosts.allow file, and
>therein is the right hostname.

>So what to do (Cant find any describtion of the error message)

Due to the help of several people (THANX) i got it:

The trick was to insert not only the hostname into the
/var/opt/advfsd/socket/hosts.allow file, but to insert the
whole host adress (name plus domain) or to insert the
IP adress of the host.


