X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078618110228

Many thanks to Glenn Newbery (glenn@bnd.com.au) (a fellow Aussie!!) for
his postscript input.

You will need to insert a line that says

statusdict /setpapertray known
{ statusdict begin 1 setpapertray end } if

This will set the paper tray to tray 1, usually the bottom tray consult
your
printer manual to confirm this. Tray 0 is the default printer tray.

We have added this postscript command into our preprocessing filter and
it now works fine.

mpage can be found on the internet under
http://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/system/printing/mpage24.tgz

